    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0729" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1 Monetary Stabilization/8: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d447-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-31T16:00:00-04:00">May 31, 1933—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. Advise Foreign Office, for the information of the Government and of the bank
                    officials, that Doctor Oliver M. W. Sprague,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d447-f2"/>
                    representative of the Government of the United States and Mr. George <pb
                        facs="0730" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/> L. Harrison, Governor of the Federal
                    Reserve Bank of New York, will sail on the SS <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Olympic</hi> on Friday, June 2nd, to discuss with British and French
                    Government representatives and representatives of their central banks methods to
                    stabilize the monetary situation.</p>
                <p>They would like to have the first meeting with the British and French Government
                    and bank representatives on the 9th in London.</p>
                <p>Please arrange for usual customs courtesies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d447-f1" n="38" type="source" xml:id="d447-f1-content">
